<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="013" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Provision + configure the Reasoning Azure OpenAI deployment</title>
    <phase>1 Platform Enablers</phase>
    <gate>done</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Infrastructure/config; appsettings + Azure deployment; may involve an external provisioning step.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Configuration + deployment coordination against a known contract; no code authoring.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Config/infra only; independent of 011/012.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>010</deps>
    <tags>azure, azure-ai, config, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Ensure a suitable Reasoning-tier Azure OpenAI deployment exists (most capable model per the north star) and
    is referenced by the StandardModel/ReasoningModel config keys added in task 010. Coordinate with whoever owns
    Azure provisioning if the deployment does not yet exist.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform engineer. Familiar with the Azure AI resources for Spaarke (see docs/architecture/auth-azure-resources.md) and appsettings binding.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The Reasoning deployment name is provisioned and set in appsettings/config so the task-010 resolver returns a
    live deployment; a smoke call to the Reasoning tier succeeds.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 010 introduces StandardModel/ReasoningModel config keys but leaves the actual deployment values to
      infra. The north star requires a genuinely more capable model for advisory reasoning. This task closes that
      loop. It may be partly external (Azure portal / IaC) — coordinate rather than block.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.json</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/auth-azure-resources.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>010 (config keys must exist to point at the deployment).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="security">Deployment names/keys go through config/Key Vault; never commit secrets (CLAUDE.md §9).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Pick the most capable available reasoning-class deployment consistent with the north star and cost posture; record the choice in notes/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/architecture/auth-azure-resources.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>knowledge/azure-ai-search/</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Check whether a reasoning-class Azure OpenAI deployment already exists for the Spaarke AI resource.</step>
    <step order="2">If missing, coordinate provisioning (or provision via the standard IaC path); record the deployment name.</step>
    <step order="3">Set ReasoningModel (and StandardModel/Fast) config values; keep secrets in Key Vault.</step>
    <step order="4">Smoke-test: a Reasoning-tier Action returns a completion from the reasoning deployment.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 013 ✅ (or blocked-external with owner + ETA if provisioning is out of band).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If provisioning requires spend approval or an Azure change outside this repo's control, mark blocked-external and escalate to the owner rather than stalling dependent tasks.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Azure CLI / config.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.json (Reasoning deployment reference)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The task-010 resolver returns a live, reachable Reasoning deployment name from config.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A smoke call on the Reasoning tier returns a valid completion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No secret is committed; deployment reference is in config/Key Vault.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    This can run alongside 011/012. If external provisioning lags, downstream tasks can develop against the
    Standard deployment and switch on merge.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
